-- title:
--   Vélu's explicit 2-isogeny equals the translate-sum map
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be a field with $2 \neq 0$ and let $W$ be a Weierstrass curve over $F$, with coefficients $a_1,a_2,a_3,a_4,a_6$. Let $(x_0,y_0)$ be a nonsingular point of the associated affine curve `W.toAffine`, and write $Q$ for the corresponding point `Affine.Point.some x₀ y₀ hns` of the group of points. Assume $W.\mathrm{veluGy}(x_0,y_0) = -(2y_0 + a_1x_0 + a_3) = 0$, and put $g_x = W.\mathrm{veluGx}(x_0,y_0) = 3x_0^2 + 2a_2x_0 + a_4 - a_1y_0$; assume further that the curve `W.veluQuotient2 x₀ y₀`, with the same $a_1,a_2,a_3$ and with $a_4$ replaced by $a_4 - 5g_x$ and $a_6$ by $a_6 - b_2 g_x - 7x_0 g_x$, has nonzero discriminant. Let $P$ be a point of `W.toAffine.Point` not lying in the subgroup `AddSubgroup.zmultiples Q` of integer multiples of $Q$. Then the pair `coordsOrZero` of the image of $P$ under [`WeierstrassCurve.veluPointMap2`](def/WeierstrassCurve_VeluPointMap2.html#L95) (which sends the point at infinity and every affine point with $x$-coordinate $x_0$ to the point at infinity of the quotient curve, and any other affine point $(x,y)$ to the point with coordinates `velu2X`, `velu2Y`) equals, componentwise, the value of the translate-sum expression $\bigl(\mathrm{pr}_i P + \sum_{k \in [1,2-1]} (\mathrm{pr}_i(P + kQ) - \mathrm{pr}_i(kQ))\bigr)$ for $i = 1,2$, where $\mathrm{pr}_i$ denotes the $i$-th component of `coordsOrZero`, this function sending the point at infinity to $(0,0)$ and an affine point to its coordinate pair. The index set $[1,2-1]$ is the singleton $\{1\}$, so the right-hand side is $\bigl(x(P) + x(P+Q) - x_0,\ y(P) + y(P+Q) - y_0\bigr)$.
--
--   This identifies, for a kernel generated by a point of order two, Vélu's explicit quotient formula with the translate-sum formula $X = x + \sum_{R \neq 0} (x(P+R) - x(R))$, $Y = y + \sum_{R \neq 0}(y(P+R) - y(R))$ over the nontrivial points $R$ of the kernel. It is used in the treatment of supersingular level data and of Hecke correspondences on modular curves, where the degeneracy maps are described through the translate-sum presentation.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_WeierstrassCurve_coordsOrZero_veluPointMap2.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_WeierstrassCurve_VeluPointMap2
import Definitions.Def_WeierstrassCurve_OddOrderSummingSet

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

theorem WeierstrassCurve.coordsOrZero_veluPointMap2
    {F : Type*} [Field F] [DecidableEq F] (W : WeierstrassCurve F) (h2 : (2 : F) ≠ 0)
    {x₀ y₀ : F} (hns : W.toAffine.Nonsingular x₀ y₀) (hgy : W.veluGy x₀ y₀ = 0)
    (hΔ : (W.veluQuotient2 x₀ y₀).Δ ≠ 0)
    (P : W.toAffine.Point)
    (hP : P ∉ AddSubgroup.zmultiples (WeierstrassCurve.Affine.Point.some x₀ y₀ hns : W.toAffine.Point)) :
    (WeierstrassCurve.veluPointMap2 h2 hns.1 hgy hΔ P).coordsOrZero =
      (P.coordsOrZero.1 + ∑ k ∈ Finset.Icc 1 (2 - 1),
          ((P + k • (WeierstrassCurve.Affine.Point.some x₀ y₀ hns : W.toAffine.Point)).coordsOrZero.1 -
            (k • (WeierstrassCurve.Affine.Point.some x₀ y₀ hns : W.toAffine.Point)).coordsOrZero.1),
       P.coordsOrZero.2 + ∑ k ∈ Finset.Icc 1 (2 - 1),
          ((P + k • (WeierstrassCurve.Affine.Point.some x₀ y₀ hns : W.toAffine.Point)).coordsOrZero.2 -
            (k • (WeierstrassCurve.Affine.Point.some x₀ y₀ hns : W.toAffine.Point)).coordsOrZero.2)) := by sorry
